# MQ14 "Great Gate". MQ13 100 set MQ14 10: the Great Gate is open and a siege engine crawls toward it. The player
# enters (MQ14.inGreatGate), reaches the Great Sigil Stone before the 15 minutes run out and takes it (45); back
# outside Bruma the script sets 48 and 50. Martin's greeting takes the Stone (60 -> 100), which starts MQ15 at 10.
# DRAFT from tools/live/quest_brief.py (2026-11-13): not run yet.

# The Great Gate (MQ13Gate4, MQ13OblivionGate4Script OnActivate): entering sets MQ14.inGreatGate, so Martin is
# not killed for the player's absence.
# (entering the Great Gate is the end of mq13_battle, in 1200)

# The run to the Great Sigil Stone is the player's race against the siege engine: moveto stands in. Activating the
# Stone (MQ14SigilStone, MQ14SigilStoneScript) sets 45, gives MQ14GreatSigilStoneItem and closes the Gate; with
# the player back at Bruma MQ14Script sets 48 and, 5 s later, 50.
case mq14_great_sigil_stone
run
player.moveto MQ14SigilStone
wait 120
activate MQ14SigilStone
until 600 GetStage MQ14 >= 45
until 1800 player.GetItemCount MQ14GreatSigilStoneItem >= 1
until 3600 GetStage MQ14 >= 48
expect MartinRef.GetDead == 0
until 600 GetStage MQ14 >= 50
expect GetStageDone MQ14 40 == 0
end

# Martin on the battlefield: his greeting at 50 ("We won a great victory here today! ...", INFO 0003D7ED) sets 60,
# whose result takes the Stone and sets 100; that sets MQ15 10.
case mq14_martin
run
player.moveto MartinRef
wait 120
approach MartinRef
talk MartinRef
until 600 GetStage MQ14 >= 60
until 300 GetStageDone MQ14 100
until 300 GetStage MQ15 >= 10
expect player.GetItemCount MQ14GreatSigilStoneItem == 0
bye if open
end
